              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " dishes are the simplest things on the Persian table. This one takes its name from "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "khiar ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "khiar"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", though this version uses dill, mint and raisins in the yoghurt base. The raisins and rose water give it a lightly sweet, floral background note. Serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chill for at least 30 minutes before serving. The herbs need time to soften and flavour the yoghurt. This is not optional."
          }
        ]
      },
